.\" zvolfiles(1) — manual page, mdoc. Kept true to the program by
.\" tests/man-check.sh.
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt ZVOLFILES 1
.Os zvolrescue 0.9.7
.Sh NAME
.Nm zvolfiles
.Nd files out of ZFS filesystem datasets, without importing the pool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar global options
.Cm list
.Ar dataset
.Op Ar dev ...
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Op Ar global options
.Cm extract
.Ar dataset
.Op Ar dev ...
.Fl o Ar dir
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Op Ar global options
.Cm objects
.Ar dataset
.Op Ar dev ...
.Fl o Ar dir
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a filesystem dataset of a ZFS pool at any transaction group that
still verifies and writes its files out: directories, symbolic links,
ownership and times, each file's blocks verified by their checksums.
When the POSIX metadata is too damaged for a tree,
.Cm objects
writes one file per object instead.
Nothing is written to the members.
.Pp
The global options and the pool member options are those of
.Xr zvolrescue 1 :
.Fl f , Fl -format Ar text | json ,
.Fl v , Fl -verbose ,
.Fl q , Fl -quiet ,
.Fl -evidence-log ,
.Fl -hash-inputs ,
.Fl -no-color ,
.Fl -debug ,
.Fl -debug-log ,
and
.Fl -image ,
.Fl -hints ,
.Fl -search-order ,
.Fl -pool-guid ,
.Fl -assume-member ,
.Fl -ignore-unknown-features ,
.Fl -map ,
.Fl -device-may-fail ,
.Fl -surface-scan-on-device .
.Sh OPTIONS
Taken by every command:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -txg Ar n
Transaction group to read; the newest that verifies when absent.
.It Fl -key Ar keyspec
Dataset encryption key:
.Ql raw: Ns Ar file ,
.Ql hex: Ns Ar hex ,
.Ql passphrase: Ns Ar file ,
or
.Ql prompt .
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss list
.Nm Cm list
.Ar dataset
.Op Ar dev ...
.Op Ar options
.Pp
Show what is in the dataset.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -path Ar path
Path inside the dataset; the root when absent.
A flag rather than a trailing word: the member list is variable-length,
so a bare path after it could not be told from another member.
.It Fl R , Fl -recursive
Descend into subdirectories.
.El
.Ss extract
.Nm Cm extract
.Ar dataset
.Op Ar dev ...
.Fl o Ar dir
.Op Ar options
.Pp
Write the tree out as files.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar dir
Write the tree here.
.It Fl -path Ar path
Path inside the dataset, repeatable; everything when absent.
.It Fl -strict
Stop at the first block that cannot be read.
.It Fl -preserve Ar list
Metadata to restore: any of
.Ql times ,
.Ql mode ,
comma-separated; default both.
.El
.Ss objects
.Nm Cm objects
.Ar dataset
.Op Ar dev ...
.Fl o Ar dir
.Op Ar options
.Pp
One file per object, for when the POSIX metadata is gone.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar dir
Write the objects here.
.It Fl -strict
Stop at the first block that cannot be read.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
As in
.Xr zvolrescue 1 :
0 success, 1 usage (a missing key among it), 2 evidence unreadable, 3
the dataset unreadable at the requested TXG, 4 not every file whole, 5
refused, 6 interrupted by a signal, 7 the medium refused a read.
.Sh EXAMPLES
One directory of a home dataset, at the TXG before it was emptied:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zvolfiles list pool/home /dev/ada0p3 /dev/ada1p3 -R --txg 4816229
zvolfiles extract pool/home /dev/ada0p3 /dev/ada1p3 --txg 4816229 \e
    --path alice/thesis -o /mnt/rescue/home
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zvolcarve 1 ,
.Xr zvolreport 1 ,
.Xr zvolrescue 1 ,
.Xr zvoltimeline 1
